      "status": "accepted",
      "explanation": "Replace per\u2011value stringstream conversion with integer digit extraction. The original code streams each integer into an ostringstream, creates a temporary string, and iterates its characters to sum ASCII codes. Since values are bounded (0\u2011999), we can compute the same sum directly by extracting decimal digits with modulo/division, adding '0'+digit for each digit. This eliminates dynamic memory allocation and heavy iostream work, reducing runtime while preserving exact observable checksum behavior.",
